DCC - forked into devsys on 2026-10-02 from ~/projects/dcc/CoCoC
(Source/Compiler/{CPP,CC09,COpt,DCC}): commit 68fdbf9 plus the owner's
uncommitted changes in that working tree, saved as uncommitted-at-fork.patch
(CPP dues.c/lex.c/parse.c, COpt inst.c/labels.c/optim.c, CC09/GNUmakefile,
DCC/dcc.c). Left out: object files, built binaries, and the *-orig.c /
*-old.c backup copies. No upstream history kept.

Build each part with "make -f GNUmakefile" in CPP, CC09, COpt and DCC.
harness/dccdiff.py compares this build with CoCoC's on every C source.

Changes (phase 6, docs/DESIGN.md D18):
  CC09  identifiers significant to 31 characters (NAMESIZE, was 8); symbol
        entries keep room for 8 and grow only for longer names; full names
        in the assembly; fixed: getword's buffer overflow, settype leaving
        the dimension list unset and an unterminated dimension chain
        (crash on XLisp/xlkmap.c)
  COpt  labels up to 32 characters (LABELSIZE, was 11); fixed: "puls u"
        read two bytes before its operand
  DCC   runs las instead of rma

Changes (phase 7, native build; docs/DESIGN.md D20, D25):
  CC09  on OS-9, allocates with sbrk instead of ibrk (cj.h ALLOCATE), so
        dcc68 can start with a small data area and grow: the F256 won't
        fork a 6-block module with more than 8K of initial data
  COpt  "#define void int" on OS-9 (op.h): DCC itself has no void
Changes (phase 10; docs/DESIGN.md D33):
  CC09  a char function's result used as a condition (if (f()), while,
        ?:) is tested with tstb, not "std -2,s": the callee sets only B
        (bool.c checkop). Inherited from CoCoC; dccdiff unchanged
Changes (2026-10-07; docs/DESIGN.md D39; also made in the CoCoC tree):
  DCC   -w no longer passes -n to dcc68, which never accepted it ("unknown
        flag: -n"); on Linux runit passes each pass's exit code back
        (exit(system()) made every failure 0)
Changes (2026-10-08; docs/DESIGN.md D42):
  DCC   runs llink (our rlink fork, renamed) instead of rlink, so it never
        picks up the original rlink from PATH or /dd/CMDS

The 6809 build (../native/GNUmakefile) compiles dcc68 with -s and
without -DPROF so it stays at most 48,384 bytes (6 blocks ending by $FD00);
it is 48,355 now.
Design and roadmap: ../docs/DESIGN.md
